# TypeScript source is text by definition, so say so rather than letting git
# guess. src/person-overlay.ts holds a NUL — the separator in rowKey, where a
# space would collide because a display_name can contain one — and git's
# heuristic reads that one byte as "binary" and refuses to diff the file.
#
# The NUL is correct and stays; what changes is git's guess about it. Scoped to
# the language, not to the one file, so the next deliberate NUL does not
# silently make another file unreviewable (beeline-e3q).
*.ts  diff
*.tsx diff
